<title>UK: ICI sets $500 million five-year bond.</title>
<headline>ICI sets $500 million five-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Deutsche Morgan Grenfell and UBS.  BORROWER   ICI INVEST (NETHERLANDS) BV</p>
<p>GUARANTOR  IMPERIAL CHEMICAL INDUSTRIES PLC</p>
<p> AMT    $500 MLN	COUPON     **	  MATURITY    07.AUG.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    07.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+50 BP</p>
<p> NOTES	**TO BE PRICED</p>
<p> MOODY	BAA1	LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  A-	  DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/NL</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.325     SELL CONC  1.55	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND JULY 2002 U.S. TREASURY NOTE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
